<title>ITALY: Two brokers set to trade Milan bourse from London.</title>
<headline>Two brokers set to trade Milan bourse from London.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1997-07-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Two major brokerage firms UBS and Morgan Stanley received authorisation, from Monday July 21, to trade on the Italian bourse in Milan directly from London, a Milan bourse council statement said on Friday.</p>
<p>This moved marks the first time brokers based in London will be able to trade directly in stocks on the Milan bourse.</p>
<p>The chairman of Morgan Stanley SpA in Italy Galeazzo Pecori Giolardi expressed his satisfaction at the move, and added that the move favoured the greater integration between local financial markets in Italy and other European markets.</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129052</p>
</text>
